# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit .env.local — it is gitignored.

# Canonical site origin, no trailing slash (used for metadata, sitemap, JSON-LD).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Supabase. Both come from Dashboard > Project Settings > API.
# The publishable (anon) key is safe to expose: the leads table is
# insert-only for that role, so it cannot read anything back out.
# There is deliberately no service-role key here — nothing needs one.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Lead notification email (Resend). Optional: leave blank and submissions
# still save to Supabase, they just don't get emailed — the server logs a
# warning saying so.
#
# NONE of these may take a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. That would ship the API key
# to the browser.
#
# RESEND_API_KEY   from resend.com > API Keys
# LEAD_NOTIFY_FROM must be on a domain verified in Resend, e.g.
#                  "CertLoop <notifications@certloop.net>". It cannot be a
#                  free-mail address, and it is the sender, not the
#                  recipient.
# LEAD_NOTIFY_TO   where notifications land. Defaults to CONTACT_EMAIL in
#                  src/lib/constants.ts if unset.
RESEND_API_KEY=
LEAD_NOTIFY_FROM=
LEAD_NOTIFY_TO=
